' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventProjector.java emitMessageDelta/persistAssistant
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventStream.java emitBestEffort/detachInternal
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeExecutionCoordinator.java commitTerminal
' Observed behavior: request queues may drop previews; complete events are committed first.
' Design reason: shared previews must originate before disposable HTTP queues.
' Architecture change: all new classes and connections below are pending implementation.
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 28
skinparam ranksep 40
hide empty members
top to bottom direction
title Redis Recovery - Global Target Structure\nNew classes and all connections: Pending implementation
class "Browser EventReducer\nPer Chat / connection generation" as UI
package "Mate public boundary (Pending implementation)" {
  class "ChatStreamController\nSingleton / VO boundary" as MC
  class "ChatObservationService\nSingleton" as MS
  class "AuthorizedPublicProjector\nSingleton / immutable caller context" as MP
  class "ClawObservationClient\nSingleton / protected internal API" as Client
  class "PublicHistoryRepository\nStable event identity mapping" as MH
}
package "Claw application and core" {
  class "SessionObservationController\nPending implementation / VO" as CC
  class "SessionObservationService\nPending implementation / singleton" as CS
  class "ObservationSubscription\nPending implementation / per connection\ncursor + bounded buffer" as Sub
  class "RuntimeEventProjector\nExisting extension point\nPer execution" as Runtime
  class "ExecutionPreviewAccumulator\nPending implementation / per execution" as Acc
  class "HotEventPublisher\nPending implementation / singleton" as Pub
  class "CommittedEventCatchUpService\nPending implementation / singleton" as Repair
  interface "HotEventStore\nPending implementation" as Store
  class "RedisHotEventStore\nPending implementation / singleton" as Adapter
  class "RuntimeSessionRepository\nExisting; incremental read extension pending" as Repo
}
database "Redis primary\nSnapshot + bounded Stream\nPending implementation" as Redis
database "GaussDB\nAuthoritative events and execution state" as DB
UI --> MC : authorized read / reconnect
MC --> MS : request VO
MS --> Client : private Session mapping
MS --> MP : project snapshot and events
MP --> MH : resolve stable public IDs
Client -down-> CC : independent read-only SSE
CC --> CS : authorized observation
CS "1" *-- "0..*" Sub : owns readers
Sub --> Store : snapshot at C; read after C
CS --> Repair : reconcile committed records
Runtime "1" *-- "1" Acc : accumulates before HTTP queue
Runtime --> Repo : commit complete events
Acc --> Pub : immutable preview batch
Runtime --> Pub : after database commit
Repair --> Repo : bounded committed-event read
Repair --> Pub : idempotent full-event repair
Pub --> Store : publish / checkpoint
Adapter ..|> Store
Adapter --> Redis : scripts + XREAD
Repo --> DB : short transactions
MH --> DB : public projection ownership
note bottom of Runtime
Existing database control polling is retained.
Disconnect does not cancel execution.
Redis does not restore a failed Java execution.
end note
note bottom of Store
Immutable DTOs only; no raw credentials.
New API models are proposed, not yet integrated.
Snapshot + cursor share one atomic read boundary.
end note
@enduml

@startuml redis_recovery_sequence
' Source evidence: OpenCode@fe3f3a41f79ad292cc3c7c629567385a20ec5130
' packages/protocol/src/groups/session.ts makeSessionGroup: experimental durable replay.
' packages/schema/src/session-event.ts Text.Delta and DurableDefinitions: live-only deltas.
' Design reason: a snapshot and its cursor prevent the snapshot-to-follow gap.
' Java divergence: source-side Redis preview recovery is pending implementation, not observed upstream behavior.
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam maxMessageSize 160
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
hide footbox
title Browser Reopen - Target Recovery\nPending implementation
actor Browser
participant "Mate replica B" as Mate
participant "Claw reader C" as Reader
database "Shared Redis" as Redis
participant "Claw executor A" as Exec
database "Authoritative DB" as DB
== Execution survives browser disconnect ==
Browser -> Browser : close page
note over Mate,Reader : Read subscriptions close; executor is not canceled.
Exec -> Exec : accumulate projected text
Exec -> Redis : atomic batch + full preview + cursor
== Reopen on any authorized replica ==
Browser -> Mate : GET public Chat stream
Mate -> Mate : authenticate / authorize / map Chat
Mate -> Reader : independent internal GET stream
Reader -> Redis : atomic snapshot read
Redis --> Reader : preview + cursor C
Exec -> Redis : append batch C+1
Reader --> Mate : initial snapshot
Mate --> Browser : public preview snapshot
Browser -> Browser : replace incomplete previews only
Reader -> Redis : XREAD after C
Redis --> Reader : batch C+1 (not lost)
Reader --> Mate : normalized delta
Mate --> Browser : public delta
Browser -> Mate : GET complete history
Mate -> DB : authorized public projection / reconciliation
DB --> Mate : complete events
Mate --> Browser : complete history
Browser -> Browser : deduplicate; completed wins
== Finish or continue ==
Exec -> DB : commit complete message
Exec -> Redis : publish completed; remove preview
Redis --> Reader : completed notification
Reader --> Mate : complete event
Mate --> Browser : same public eventId / completed
note over Browser,DB
No automatic POST replay. No sticky sessions for readers.
Redis failure uses history fallback, not a zero-loss promise.
Executor failure requires a separate recovery design.
end note
@enduml
